Chapter: Random

 The Random effect provides random-integer.
 To random-integer gives a random Integer between the given lower and upper bounds inclusive.

 We say:

Section: Definitions

  effect Random where
    random-integer : Integer, Integer -> [Random] Integer

Section: Deterministic Mixing

 This chapter declared the effect and supplied no way to compute anything, so
 every chapter that wanted pseudo-randomness wrote its own mixer in place.
 Measured 2026-07-25, ten of them, and all the same shape: a multiply by an
 odd constant, sometimes an add, sometimes an xor of two such products.

 Multiplication and addition carry entropy UPWARD only. Bit i of a product
 depends on bits 0..i of its inputs and on nothing above them, so the low bits
 of every one of those mixers are a function of the low bits of the inputs.
 Any caller that then takes a remainder by a small range, or masks off low
 bits, gets structure rather than noise.

 The GA's was the measured case. ga-rand-range at range 2 reduced to
 lowbit(seed) XOR lowbit(idx), so ga-random-population produced thirty
 chromosomes with an identical alternating gene pattern and identical fitness.

 The failure is invisible to the obvious test. Over 256 consecutive indices
 the old mixer's low bit is 128 ones out of 256 -- perfectly balanced -- and
 255 alternations out of 255, which is the comb 0101... and carries no
 information at all. Only a serial-correlation check can see it; a balance
 check certifies it.

 mix-bits is the standard remedy: multiply to spread, then xor-shift the high
 bits back down so the low ones inherit them. Same construction as the
 SplitMix64 finalizer. Deterministic and pure, which is what a seeded
 simulation, a hash table and a reproducible test all need. True entropy is a
 different problem and belongs to the Random EFFECT above, not here.

 THE MISSING FOLD IS ONLY A DEFECT WHERE THE CONSUMER READS LOW BITS, and
 that qualification is worth more than the rule it qualifies. Measure the
 consumer, never the mixer.

 A remainder by a power of two, or a bit-and against a mask, reads the low
 bits and nothing else, so an unfolded mixer is degenerate there. A small
 modulus is nearly as bad. But a remainder by a large non-power-of-two
 samples the whole word and pulls the high bits back in by itself, and an
 unfolded mixer can be perfectly adequate.

 Measured 2026-07-25, same unfolded shape, opposite verdicts:

   CountMinSketch  mod 64 (a power of two)   24 of 40 keys overestimated
   Reservoir       mod n, n small            item counts 12 against 78
   CardDeck        mod (i+1), i descending   a two-card deck striped 255/255
   Steering        mod 6283                  bins 26 33 32 31 31 32 33 38
   ImageTensor     / 2147484                 bins 31 32 30 31 25 42 31 34

 The last two are FINE and were both recorded as broken on the strength of
 their expressions before anyone ran them. Steering's modulus is not a power
 of two, so the remainder samples the whole word. ImageTensor's
 `bit-and raw 2147483647` is the LCG's MODULUS rather than its output
 extraction -- the output is `next / 2147484`, which reads the high bits, and
 an LCG's high bits are its good ones.

 Four chapters were graded broken by reading them. Two of the four were
 wrong. Reading a mixer and grading it is a guess; running the consumer and
 counting is the answer, and the guess was wrong half the time.

  mix-bits : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mix-bits (seed) (idx) =
    let z = seed * 2654435769 + idx * 1442695040888963407
    in let a = bit-xor z (bit-shru z 30)
    in let b = a * 6364136223846793005
    in let c = bit-xor b (bit-shru b 27)
    in let d = c * 1442695040888963407
    in bit-xor d (bit-shru d 31)

 rand-in-range answers a value in [lo, hi] inclusive. The absolute value is
 taken after mixing, not before, because it is the mixed bits that need to be
 uniform.

  rand-in-range : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rand-in-range (seed) (idx) (lo) (hi) =
    let h = mix-bits seed idx
    in let positive = if h < 0 then -h else h
    in let range = hi - lo + 1
    in if range <= 0 then lo
    else lo + (positive - (positive / range) * range)

